       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nThe 1700 mg dose may be a typo. Here are some options within the labeled limits:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is a more typical starting or titration dose.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you meant a different drug or formulation, tell me that too."
